{"title":"The chain rule, run by a computer","sub":"Backpropagation on a small graph, then on a deep network.","kind":"graph","interval":2600,"scenarioLabel":"Show","graph":{"w":400,"h":200,"r":20,"nodes":[{"id":"x","x":40,"y":100,"label":"x","sub":"below"},{"id":"a","x":140,"y":50,"label":"+1","sub":"below"},{"id":"b","x":245,"y":50,"label":"x²","sub":"below"},{"id":"c","x":190,"y":150,"label":"sin","sub":"below"},{"id":"y","x":355,"y":100,"label":"×","sub":"below"}],"edges":[{"u":"x","v":"a","dir":true},{"u":"a","v":"b","dir":true},{"u":"b","v":"y","dir":true},{"u":"x","v":"c","dir":true},{"u":"c","v":"y","dir":true}]},"scenarios":[{"name":"Forward and backward","frames":[{"caption":"Forward pass for y = (x + 1)² · sin x at x = 1. Each node computes its value from its inputs, left to right, and stores it.","nodes":{"x":{"sub":"x = 1","cls":"a"},"a":{"sub":""},"b":{"sub":""},"c":{"sub":""},"y":{"sub":""}},"edges":{},"stats":[["Pass","forward"]]},{"caption":"a = x + 1 = 2, then b = a² = 4. Separately, c = sin x ≈ 0.841.","nodes":{"x":{"sub":"x = 1","cls":"a"},"a":{"sub":"a = 2","cls":"a"},"b":{"sub":"b = 4","cls":"a"},"c":{"sub":"c = 0.841","cls":"a"},"y":{"sub":""}},"edges":{"x-a":"a","a-b":"a","x-c":"a"},"stats":[["Pass","forward"]]},{"caption":"y = b · c ≈ 3.366. The forward pass is done. Now the backward pass. Write g for each node's gradient ∂y/∂(node), and start from g = 1 at the output.","nodes":{"x":{"sub":"x = 1","cls":"a"},"a":{"sub":"a = 2","cls":"a"},"b":{"sub":"b = 4","cls":"a"},"c":{"sub":"c = 0.841","cls":"a"},"y":{"sub":"y = 3.366, g = 1","cls":"b"}},"edges":{"b-y":"a","c-y":"a"},"stats":[["Pass","backward"]]},{"caption":"At the × node, each input's gradient is the other input: ∂y/∂b = c ≈ 0.841 and ∂y/∂c = b = 4. These use the values stored in the forward pass.","nodes":{"x":{"sub":"x = 1","cls":"a"},"a":{"sub":"a = 2","cls":"a"},"b":{"sub":"b = 4, g = 0.841","cls":"b"},"c":{"sub":"c = 0.841, g = 4","cls":"b"},"y":{"sub":"y = 3.366, g = 1","cls":"b"}},"edges":{"b-y":"b","c-y":"b"},"stats":[["Pass","backward"]]},{"caption":"Keep going right to left, multiplying by each node's local derivative. Through the square: ∂y/∂a = 2a · ∂y/∂b ≈ 3.366.","nodes":{"x":{"sub":"x = 1","cls":"a"},"a":{"sub":"a = 2, g = 3.366","cls":"b"},"b":{"sub":"b = 4, g = 0.841","cls":"b"},"c":{"sub":"c = 0.841, g = 4","cls":"b"},"y":{"sub":"y = 3.366, g = 1","cls":"b"}},"edges":{"a-b":"b"},"stats":[["Pass","backward"]]},{"caption":"x feeds into y along two paths. Along the top, ∂a/∂x = 1 contributes 3.366. Along the bottom, ∂c/∂x = cos x contributes 4 · cos 1 ≈ 2.161. Where paths meet, their contributions add: ∂y/∂x ≈ 5.527, which matches the product rule and a numerical check.","nodes":{"x":{"sub":"x = 1, g = 5.527","cls":"b"},"a":{"sub":"a = 2, g = 3.366","cls":"b"},"b":{"sub":"b = 4, g = 0.841","cls":"b"},"c":{"sub":"c = 0.841, g = 4","cls":"b"},"y":{"sub":"y = 3.366, g = 1","cls":"b"}},"edges":{"x-a":"b","x-c":"b"},"stats":[["Pass","backward"],["∂y/∂x","5.527"]]}],"kind":"graph"},{"name":"Vanishing gradients","kind":"plot","frames":[{"caption":"Gradient size for each layer's weights in a 30-layer network, measured by actually running backpropagation (layer 30 is next to the loss). Sigmoid activations: every layer multiplies the gradient by σ′(z) ≤ 0.25. The gradient reaching layer 1 is about 10¹⁸ times smaller than at layer 30: it has vanished.","curves":[{"tok":"muted","pts":[[1,-18.269005648547513],[2,-17.940226639135222],[3,-17.28487007304798],[4,-16.608670123351782],[5,-15.907330397137645],[6,-15.277679336458819],[7,-14.694585069095314],[8,-14.077546056966794],[9,-13.484272796756903],[10,-12.863335779448606],[11,-12.218625825559492],[12,-11.577035067026646],[13,-10.947222289982285],[14,-10.340989947231916],[15,-9.717296779611857],[16,-9.052267534115733],[17,-8.372210598936585],[18,-7.76226667045511],[19,-7.008969588267489],[20,-6.435015392440408],[21,-5.747603360830006],[22,-5.2000190165032985],[23,-4.519811342501259],[24,-3.946470